During the pandemic, my team had the privilege of taking part in immersive Agile Dojo training. We were already a high-performing team, but wow, did our performance accelerate after Dojo!

By now, you've probably heard of Given-When-Then (GWT). If you aren't using this format yet, keep reading, because I'm going to convince you that you need to use it!  
GWT not only provides developers a clear understanding of the work, but also provides QA a roadmap for testing- if done well that is!  


This is generic example for a Help Request modules in an application.

**NEW FUNCTIONALITY**

GIVEN I log into the Pack application
WHEN the screen displays
THEN I see the New Request button

GIVEN I click the New Request button
WHEN the click the reason from the drop down 
THEN I see the following options
* Supplies
* Clean up/Item spilled
* Technical Support
* Login Errors

GIVEN I select a reason
WHEN I click submit
THEN I see confirmation my request was submitted





